<%#
  Admin-only: deployment-state card. Phase 2 — wires up after the v0.16
  devnet deploy + Carl's Solana::Vault refactor. Right now the cells are
  placeholders explaining what each field will show.

  PHASE 2 HOOK POINTS — when wiring live data, the controller should
  set @vault_state via Solana::Vault.cached_vault_state (already exists
  for v0.15.1, signature will stay the same after Carl's refactor) and
  populate:
    @vault_paused              # bool
    @accepted_currencies       # Array<AcceptedCurrency> filtered to active
    @op_rev_balances           # Hash<currency_idx => u64>
  Then replace the <dd> "—" placeholders below with the real values.
%>
<section class="card border-2 border-primary/30 p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-4 mb-2">
    <h2 class="text-heading font-bold text-xl">Live deployment state</h2>
    <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-primary uppercase tracking-wider">admin only</span>
  </div>
  <p class="text-warning text-sm mb-5 max-w-3xl">
    Phase 2 &mdash; wires up after the live-state Rails refactor. Fields below are placeholders so the layout
    is ready when Carl's Rails refactor lands.
  </p>

  <dl class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

    <div class="bg-surface-alt border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-1">Program ID</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-heading break-all">
        <%# Phase 2: read from Solana::Config::PROGRAM_ID at request time.

            THE FALLBACK IS A LOAD FAILURE, NOT A MISSING VAR. Scope: the
            THREE RESCUED values, which live in TWO of this card's six cells.
            This cell reads Solana::Config, and so do both halves of the
            Upgrade authority cell below. The other four cells (Paused,
            Registered currencies, Operator revenue, Treasury authority) are
            Phase 2 placeholders bound for the vault-state preload named in the
            header above, not for Solana::Config, and carry no rescue yet.

            None of the three env vars behind the Config reads can reach a
            RENDERED page unset. PROGRAM_ID and NETWORK are load-time constants
            that raise during eager load in production (OPSEC-012; for NETWORK,
            unset, empty and whitespace-only alike), so a missing value stops
            boot instead of showing up here; dev and test resolve both to
            devnet defaults and cannot raise at all; and squads_vault_pda never
            raises in any environment. The only trigger left for these rescues
            is Solana::Config itself failing to resolve.

            AND THE THIRD IS NEVER SEEN - BUT IT DOES FIRE. The application
            layout reads Solana::Config.devnet? on the body tag of EVERY render,
            unrescued (layouts/application.html.erb, the data-solana-cluster
            attribute), and devnet? reads NETWORK. ActionView renders the
            template and its partials FIRST and the layout SECOND: in
            template_renderer.rb the layout is stored as
            view_flow.set(:layout, yield(layout)) and only then rendered. So the
            true sequence is that this partial renders, the NETWORK rescue below
            FIRES, and then the layout raises and the fully-rendered body is
            DISCARDED. Measured both ways: instrumenting
            render_partial.action_view during a failing request shows this
            partial completing with exception nil and the layout carrying the
            NameError, and rendering this partial standalone with NETWORK
            removed returns 3,569 bytes with the fallback string in the output.

            So the message below says unreachable, which is true of what a
            reader can SEE, and it must not claim the partial never ran.

            Each message names the state that actually produces it, plus what
            is true of its own value, so a reader is not sent chasing a
            variable that is fine. %>
        <%= (Solana::Config::PROGRAM_ID rescue "(Solana::Config did not load; an unset SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID stops boot instead)") %>
      </dd>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1">Same on devnet + mainnet builds &mdash; pinned via SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-1">Upgrade authority</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-heading break-all">
        <%# Read from Solana::Config at request time. PER CLUSTER, unlike the program ID above:
            devnet and mainnet are different Squads, so this must never be a literal.

            The message states the unset case as a CONDITION rather than a fact
            about right now. The variable is absent on both deployed apps today,
            but config.rb keeps the env override as the runbook escape hatch, so
            the first legitimate use of that hatch must not make this line print
            a false sentence. %>
        <%= (Solana::Config.squads_vault_pda rescue "(Solana::Config did not load; with SOLANA_SQUADS_VAULT_PDA unset, as it is on both deployed apps, the cluster default is the live path)") %>
      </dd>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1">Squads V4 2-of-3 vault PDA on <%= (Solana::Config::NETWORK rescue "an unresolved cluster (this fallback is unreachable: it renders, then the layout reads NETWORK too and raises, so the whole body is discarded unseen)") %> &mdash; each cluster has its own Squad. Only the Squad can ship upgrades.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-1">Paused</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">
        <%# Phase 2: replace with @vault_state&.paused ? "yes" : "no". %>
        &mdash; <span class="text-[11px] text-muted">live data, wires after deploy</span>
      </dd>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1">Read from VaultState.paused via the cached vault-state preload.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-1">Registered currencies</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">
        <%# Phase 2: iterate @accepted_currencies, render mint + active flag. %>
        &mdash; <span class="text-[11px] text-muted">live data, wires after deploy</span>
      </dd>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1">accepted_currencies[16], filtered to active = true.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-1">Operator revenue (USDC)</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">
        <%# Phase 2: @op_rev_balances[0] formatted as dollars. %>
        &mdash; <span class="text-[11px] text-muted">live data, wires after deploy</span>
      </dd>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1">Balance in the per-currency op_rev ATA. Sweepable to Squads vault.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt border border-subtle rounded-lg p-4">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-1">Treasury authority</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-xs text-muted break-all">
        <%# Phase 2: pull from @vault_state&.treasury_authority once the field exists. %>
        &mdash; <span class="text-[11px] text-muted">pinned at initialize</span>
      </dd>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1">Destination owner for sweep_operator_revenue. Set once, immutable.</p>
    </div>

  </dl>
</section>
